{
  "$comment": "One rule set for both pre-flight sandboxes: apps/orchestrator/src/preflight/local.ts (via packages/catalog/src/preflight-rules.ts) and modal-sandbox/contextpane_sandbox.py (copied into the Modal image). Every rule here is a hard failure. A command passes only if its verb is in readOnlyVerbs, or it is in allowedCommands, or the bundle's steered contract allows it (the scenario's or strategy's required commands, never the coder's own list), or the script defines it as a function. Commands without a hyphen (native binaries such as pwsh, az, bash, curl) fail unless they are harmless pipeline aliases. privilegedPatterns name commands that grant roles, credentials, app permissions or code execution: they are never in allowedCommands and pass only through a steered contract. inverseCommands are what the repository's own inverse rollbacks use; they are never allowed in a forward bundle. Command names are lower-case; destructivePatterns and privilegedPatterns are case-insensitive regular expressions valid in JavaScript and Python. deniedExecutionCommands are applied by the execution-surface rules (apps/orchestrator/src/preflight/execution-surface.ts). The executor connects before the script runs (apps/orchestrator/src/execution/executor-identity.ts), so Connect-/Disconnect- of Graph and Az are denied. forbiddenPatterns are case-insensitive regular expressions over the whole script (strings included): a password reset or disabling a policy fail whatever command carries them.",
